ased  on the hero that you pick with each hero  having its own corresponding storyline  make sure to go check it out today and  thank you naraka bladepoint for  sponsoring this video  so our first group of interesting  discoveries has to do with the merchants  that are randomly spread throughout the  game some musicians in my most recent  stream pointed out that the merchants  who have this violin-like instrument are  apparently accurately playing the  instrument meaning that the hand  movements motions and animations are  almost exactly how you would accurately  play this style of instrument in real  life each change in the tone of the  music being played is followed with an  accurate change in hand position take a  look  [Music]  also the music here is apparently  playing tribute to german's boss theme  from bloodborne it's not exactly the  same but definitely sounds similar  enough to take notice of i'll show you a  comparison now  [Music]  the corrupted merchant in the cathedral  of the forsaken is also playing music  but i haven't been able to figure out if  this song is playing tribute to anything  in my opinion it's likely just sad music  that the developers put here as a joke  because they knew that they designed the  most difficult platforming section in  the game in this location so at least  we're being soothed with relaxing music  while we follow our deaths over and over  again final weird thing about the  merchants but a couple of them have very  suspect and funny sounding laughs after  being killed  oh  could you  what have i ever done  speaking of death sounds and dialogue  and i am so so sorry to everyone out  there for doing this but muriel's  dialogue after being attacked is  actually quite interesting in addition  muriel has a massive health bar for  being a non-boss which makes sense when  he tells us that he can't be wounded or  die stop it please  my flesh is akin to stone i cannot be  wounded  i cannot die  but nor will i cause any harm unto you  cease your futile efforts  if you talk to him after attacking him  he will make you feel so bad about  yourself it reminds me of a disappointed  dad with some very wise words  are you quite finished take this  opportunity to learn to master your  emotions  worry not i take no offense  but others are not always so forgiving  some take to anger  others sorrow  bonds are fragile things  won't to break under strain  and once they're broken  everything is lost  with not to gain and if you're still  curious yes muriel can die it is  absolutely horrible and i feel awful  about myself for even getting a clip of  this i did it so you don't have to  regarding more on this area is the  church of vows where we just murdered  muriel is this statue where you can  offer celestial due to atone for your  sins most players already know this but  if you didn't you can use this just in  case you've antagonized an npc and can't  continue their quest line you can atone  for your sins here the npc will forgive  you and you can then resume that quest  line just know it doesn't fully work if  you fully kill an npc they are gone  forever if you do that  however i found this exact same statue  in noxtella which is conveniently  located directly below the church of  vows this statue is clearly representing  the nox which their armor set reads that  they had been banished by the greater  will to the deep underground where they  now live under a false night sky and  await a new age of the coming stars and  their lord of night if we read about the  celestial dew that we can offer this  knox statue it tells us that once upon a  time the stars of the night sky guided  fate and this is a recollection of those  times this reminds me of ronnie's  questline which actively tells us that  her fate is guided by the stars stay  tuned for a potential lore video on this  subject and let me know what you think  as well next up is this sound effect  from the flame of frenzy outside the  frenzied flame village there's a very  unique sound here that i can't quite put  my finger on sometimes when i listen  very closely it's almost like there's a  woman singing or humming very quietly in  the background of this normally very  chaotic in-game moment maybe i'm just  hearing things and it's intentionally  designed to make a chaotic sound which  would fit the theme very well but take a  listen  last thing we're going to talk about  today has to do with the world map if  you haven't noticed this before there  are several locations on the map where  rune etchings are drawn onto the map  some of these are written over what  looks like labeled banners already drawn  onto the map but other rune drawings can  be seen in random locations as well  there's a possibility that there's a  hidden language within the game my  stream and i even tried to decipher  these rune letters but obviously failed  miserably in doing so runes like this  can be seen in many different ways  throughout the game so hopefully someone  smarter than myself could potentially  determine if this really is a language  that can be translated somehow that  could really help in a lot of avenues of  discovery throughout the game if that's  possible but i really doubt it also in  regards to the map if you're like me  you've been very curious about this  middle section of the map that has this  ominous cloud drawn in here i originally  thought this was just to fill space for  an otherwise empty part of the map  that's just the ocean but when i zoomed  in closer i found it very interesting  that they just left a giant unfilled  texture block in this location obviously  without the use of this camera tool the  player would never be able to notice  this so it could just be an oversight i  still find it very odd and it makes me  think that something may have been here  at some point in development but was  otherwise just cut out another  interesting area on this map is up to  the north where we can see this meteor  drawn onto the map that is seemingly  crash-landed into the ocean here however  when we try to take a closer look at  this location there is no meteor to be  found there are these weird triangular  textures that are seemingly just left  here it really just makes me think that  there was originally something here and  was just cut out of the game later in  production but also could just be an  oversight in an area that will never be  naturally seen by the player again let  me know what you guys think about all of  this stuff and that's all i've got for  you today thank you for watching the  video huge shout out again to naraka  bladepoint for sponsoring the video it  helps the channel out a ton make sure to  check the pin comment below to  potentially win a 50 amazon gift card if  you do want it other than that i will  see you all in the next video take care
 

